      "value": "@{5a4aaf7f758fa46d131cd36b|full_name}: No, your hand position doesn't actually affect anything during the lock in phase. You can place your hands and head literally anywhere and it will have zero effect. Only the feet and hips matter. The head and hands will always reference the head and hand bones directly same as in normal VR.\n\nGuzuo is correct that shoulder movement is quite different between normal VR and full body. It's common to notice a lot more clipping around the shoulders when using an avatar in full body due to the sharper bends it causes.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
